<title>USA: Cephalon,Chiron FDA review extended.</title>
<headline>Cephalon,Chiron FDA review extended.</headline>
<dateline>WEST CHESTER, Pa. 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cephalon Inc and Chiron Corp said Monday that the U.S. Food and Drug Administation has extended its review period for the new drug application submitted for clearance to market Myotrophin.</p>
<p>The review period has been extended until November 11, the companies said.</p>
<p>Myotrophin, an injection, is used to treat amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, commonly referred to as Lou Gehrig's disease.</p>
<p>Cephalon and Chiron submitted the NDA on February 11, and recently submitted an amendment to the NDA, which entitles the FDA to extend its review deadline by three months.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
